ATS-301 / review item 1 (C1) -- Playwright's positional test filter
================================================================

THE DEFECT
  hasPositionalFilter() only understood a FULL `--help` text. The adapter
  however probes the CLI and already extracts the bare USAGE line, then
  handed THAT to the check. The check found no 'Usage:' prefix, parsed
  nothing, and reported filterByFile as unsupported -- a false negative on
  a capability the adapter uses on every filtered run.

THE FIX
  server/adapters/contract.mjs -- hasPositionalFilter() now accepts either the
  full help text or the already-extracted bare usage line; a bare usage line
  is matched directly against the positional-filter marker.

--- PROOF 1: the real Playwright project reports filterByFile supported ---
command: node --test --test-name-pattern=IT-ADP-005 tests/adapters-it.test.mjs
exit code: 0
  ✔ IT-ADP-005: negotiation over the real Playwright project proves the CLI options (413.835ms)
  ✔ IT-ADP-005B: the real Playwright CLI declares a positional test filter (815.9371ms)
  ✔ IT-ADP-005C: the real Playwright run passes the filtered file as a positional argument (415.9683ms)
  ℹ tests 3
  ℹ pass 3
  ℹ fail 0
  ℹ skipped 0

  IT-ADP-005B asserts, over the REAL @playwright/test project:
    - cap.supported === true
    - cap.reason === ''            (a supported capability carries no reason)
    - cap.evidence quotes the SAME usage line the capability came from
    - cap.detail.usage matches /\[test-filter/i
    - requireCapability(a, project, ['filterByFile']) does NOT raise
  IT-ADP-005C asserts the claim matches the EXECUTION: the file reaches
  the CLI as the last POSITIONAL argument, never as an option.

--- PROOF 2: the negative case -- a usage line WITHOUT a test filter ---
  tools/test_wbs_common.py style unit coverage in tests/adapters.test.mjs
  (UT-ADP-017) and tests/adapters-engines.test.mjs (UT-PWA-004) use a
  FORGED probe whose usage text has no test-filter marker and assert the
  capability is NOT supported.

--- PROOF 3: the positive tests are NOT constant -- mutation ---
  server/adapters/contract.mjs -- the positional-filter match is disabled
  (the check is forced to 'no positional filter'), i.e. the pre-fix
  behaviour. The real-project assertions must then go red.
